    "text": "The refactoring has been implemented. Here's a summary of the design and the complete code.\n\n## Design Overview\n\n**Package layout** (`bench/` package plus two standalone analysis tools):\n\n```\nbench/\n  __init__.py            # public API re-exports\n  config.py              # BenchmarkConfig, CaseConfig, strict validation\n  supervisor.py          # EngineProcess / GPUMonitor / ProcessSupervisor\n  artifacts.py           # ArtifactWriter (manifests, logs, requests.json)\n  runner.py              # run_benchmark() \u2014 CLI entry point\n  analysis.py            # parse_rounds, summarize_rows, build_report\ntools/\n  analyze_window_union.py  # refactored analyzer (same semantics, testable)\n  test_analyze_window_union.py\n  check_verify_scratch.py  # refactored parity harness\ntests/\n  test_supervisor.py\n  test_runner.py\n```\n\n**Key decisions:**\n\n1. **`ProcessSupervisor`** \u2014 a single context manager owning every child process (engine, GPU monitor, watchdog). It uses `threading.Timer` for the deadline, registers `atexit` and signal handlers, and guarantees `kill()` + `wait()` in `close()` even on exceptions or cancellation",
